<!DOCTYPE Bill PUBLIC "-//LSC//DTD Authoring Bill XML//EN" "l:\dtd\author\billauthoring.top"><Bill version="1.0" type="introLN" docName="H-0912.1"><IntroducedBillHeader><RequestNumber>H-0912.1</RequestNumber><BillNumber>HOUSE BILL 1468</BillNumber><StateLegSession><State>State of Washington</State><Legislature>58th Legislature</Legislature><Session>2003 Regular Session</Session></StateLegSession><Sponsors>Representatives Ericksen, Anderson and McMahan</Sponsors><IntroHistory><ReadDate>Read first time 01/28/2003.  </ReadDate><ReferredTo>Referred to Committee on Finance.</ReferredTo></IntroHistory></IntroducedBillHeader><BriefDescription>Providing a business and occupation tax deduction for charitable contributions.</BriefDescription><BillBody><BillTitle><LineNumber line=" 1" page="1,1" hrt="no"/>	AN ACT Relating to business and occupation tax deductions for<LineNumber line=" 2" page="1,2"/>charitable contributions; adding a new section to chapter 82.04 RCW;<LineNumber line=" 3" page="1,3"/>and providing an effective date.</BillTitle><EnactingClause><LineNumber line=" 4" page="1,4" hrt="no"/>BE IT ENACTED BY THE LEGISLATURE OF THE STATE OF WASHINGTON:</EnactingClause><BillSection type="new" clausetype="newsinglesectoch"><LineNumber line=" 5" page="1,5" hrt="no"/><BegSecNew><NewSecText>NEW SECTION.</NewSecText><SecNum>Sec. </SecNum><BegSecText>A new section is added to chapter <NewSingleSecToCh>82.04</NewSingleSecToCh> RCW<LineNumber line=" 6" page="1,6"/>to read as follows:</BegSecText><LineNumber line=" 7" page="1,7" hrt="no"/></BegSecNew><RCWSLText>	In computing tax there may be deducted from the measure of the tax<LineNumber line=" 8" page="1,8"/>any charitable contribution, as defined in section 170(c) of the<LineNumber line=" 9" page="1,9"/>internal revenue code, paid by the taxpayer during the reporting<LineNumber line="10" page="1,10"/>period.</RCWSLText></BillSection><BillSection type="new" clausetype="effectivedate"><LineNumber line="11" page="1,11" hrt="no"/><BegSecNew><NewSecText>NEW SECTION.</NewSecText><SecNum>Sec. </SecNum></BegSecNew><RCWSLText>This act takes effect January 1, 2004.</RCWSLText></BillSection><BillEnd>--- END ---<PageNumberFooter lastpage="yes">		p. 1	HB 1468</PageNumberFooter></BillEnd></BillBody></Bill>